{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791416238,"nonce":"OoZHXyP1pJbn1WfNnIEqLqIUr8g=","title":"Required fields: a required attribute on the field entity, enforced by the planner, derived from Jira's create screen","message":"Tracking only; cut from the scope of 111e8e9 on 2026-10-07 (Luis). Today nothing is required beyond type and title (schema.Checker.CheckNew, host.splitTitle). Jira's create screen marks fields required, and the sync keeps that set only in the compiled Mapping (typeMap.required, compile.go: Required \u0026\u0026 !HasDefaultValue); a create missing one is refused by Jira with a 400 and reported as failed on every run until the issue is edited (JS15). Proposal: a required bool attribute on the field entity, written as required: true in schema.yaml; CheckNew refuses a missing or null required field and CheckFields refuses clearing one, both at planning time so CLI, flows and the new view agree; the pull keeps skipping it, because required is policy and the pull checks shape only (doc/design/pull-schema-check.md); git work jira schema derives it with the same predicate the mapping uses, so the reviewed mapping carries it and the nightly re-derive follows a Jira admin's change; subtask types get parent required for free. The new view then marks required rows and Create refuses with the planner's message. Open call: whether a set to null on a required field is refused too, which is what Jira does to such a write.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["issue-model","bridge","tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"backlog","type":"task"}}]}